Statistical and nonequilibrium physics (@statistical-and-nonequilibrium-physics: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_2NCC3TE3GE2MNZB7B55QMM2JYW
Statistical physics connects microscopic states and interactions to macroscopic behaviour. This material covers ensembles, kinetic theory, phase transitions, fluctuations, transport, and driven systems, showing how collective properties emerge and how irreversible processes can be described beyond equilibrium.

**Common foundation developed:** [Microscopic states and statistical premises](../core/Specify-microscopic-states-macroscopic-questions-and-statistical-premises.lingua) begins ten lessons connecting finite ensembles, thermodynamic variables, correlations, reservoir approximations and distinct relaxation laws. Full statistical mechanics, kinetic theory, transport, phase transitions, driven systems and advanced physical investigations remain pending.

**Parent:** [Physics — fields, matter, motion and physical evidence](../Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W).
